        "STEP 1 (low risk, parity-first): inside wgmma.cuh, reimplement make_desc_{A,B}_kmajor to return a cute::GmmaDescriptor over cute::make_tensor(make_smem_ptr(p), tile_to_shape(GMMA::Layout_K_INTER_Atom<bf16>{}, Shape<Int<MN>,_16>{})).desc_ — bytes are already proven equal to the hand-packed NONE descriptor (wgmma.cuh:261-269). Keep struct SmemDesc{uint64_t desc} so call sites are untouched.",
        "STEP 2: reimplement wgmma_m64nNk16_bf16<N,ScaleD,0,0> to call MMA_64xNx16_F32BF16BF16_SS<Major::K,Major::K>::fma(dA.desc,dB.desc,acc.c[0..N/2-1],ScaleD?ScaleOut::One:ScaleOut::Zero) via the existing if-constexpr N ladder (wgmma.cuh:582-587). Reimplement wgmma_fence/commit_group/wait_group<N> as warpgroup_fence_operand(per reg)/warpgroup_commit_batch/warpgroup_wait<N>.",
        "STEP 3: KEEP WgmmaAccum<N> and wgmma_frag_decode AS-IS — the CuTe C-fragment thread->(row,col) layout is identical to the hand-decoded PTX figure (row=16*warp+lane/4+8*(within>>1), col=(lane&3)*2+(within&1)+8*(i>>2)); this guarantees the epilogue store (model_stage_decoder_tc.cuh:1090-1104) and the parity gate stay green with zero edits. Verify acc.c[i] register order matches fma's d-operand order; if CuTe orders differently, adapt the fill, not the decode.",
