      "plan_notes": [
        "Migrate exactly 3 GEMM ORIENTATIONS (all funnel through tc_gemm_block_unpipelined): (a) fwd Y=X@W^T [F1-F4], (b) dX=dY@W [X1-X4], (c) dW=dY^T@X [9 specs]. All use the same CuTe atom SM90_64xNx16_F32BF16BF16_SS<Major::K,Major::K>; only the operand SOURCES and the M/N/K role assignment differ (fwd/dX: M=tile rows=128; dW: M=Nout weight rows, K=T/B). Keep the thin orientation wrappers as the seam so the driver call sites are unchanged.",
        "fwd/dX are already on the cp.async ring (contiguous bf16, DecGmemTileSrc*) -> straightforward to swap to TMA SM90_TMA_LOAD + cutlass::pipeline producer/consumer (the PIPE=2 mbarrier engine at line 860-987 is the existing precedent to transcribe). dW DW_STAGE=1 also becomes contiguous via the pre-transpose so it can share the SAME TMA+ring; DW_STAGE=0 scalar gather and split-K keep lambda sources (no TMA) -- migrate those last or leave as fallback.",
        "PARITY-BY-CONSTRUCTION discipline: the CuTe path MUST consume the SAME bf16 operand bytes the C1/C1-T cache + dW-transpose produce (pure __float2bfloat16 of fp32 params, element-owned/deterministic). Stage them into the canonical Major-K smem positions in ascending k; issue k=0 OVERWRITE then k>0 ACCUMULATE into the fp32 accumulator. Do NOT split or reorder the k-loop (except the existing deterministic floor-balanced split-K reduce). Biases/residual adds stay in fp32 OUTSIDE the GEMM.",
        "TMA descriptor constraint: kernel owns its grid (1 CTA/SM persistent, hand-built GridBarrier) so host-launched CollectiveMma is forbidden. The TMA tensor map must be either (i) built device-side per step from the runtime acts/params/workspace pointers, or (ii) pre-built on host once and passed in -- but acts/dY/X live in the runtime workspace whose offsets depend on T=B*S, so a per-step device-side tensormap init inside P0/P1 (fenced by B0/B1) is the safer path. Budget mbarrier words + TMA descriptor smem inside DecTcSmem (watch the 48KB static / 228KB dynamic cap, gate at line 464-491).",
