      "plan_notes": [
        "Build a NEW device header composing CuTe atoms; gate behind #ifdef WITH_CUTLASS with #ifndef-fallback to the hand-rolled wgmma.cuh so the non-CUTLASS / pre-sm_90 codegen matrix still builds. The megakernel TUs csrc/fused/sm_90/*.cu already get -DWITH_CUTLASS/-DCUTLASS_NVCC_ARCHS=90a + cutlass include dir when CUTLASS is on (setup.py:683-691) — verify these flags reach the megakernel TUs (today they don't NEED cutlass).",
        "Host launcher (fused_decoder_megakernel.cuh launch_fused_decoder_megakernel_tc) builds TMA descriptor(s) BEFORE the persistent launch via make_tma_copy(SM90_TMA_LOAD{},gA/gB_tensor,SmemLayoutA/B{}) and passes get_tma_descriptor() into the kernel (add to PersistentContext or __grid_constant__ CUtensorMap). Buffers are stable-address (mma.cuh:110-117) so build-once-reuse is valid. Host slayout TYPE must equal the device smem Layout type — share a single `using` in the new header.",
        "Keep ClusterShape = Shape<_1,_1,_1> (no cluster) so the hand-built GridBarrier (megakernel_common.cuh:147-255, no cooperative launch) stays valid and PipelineTmaAsync uses the cluster_size==1 single-CTA arrival path (sm90_pipeline.hpp:311,344). DO NOT introduce SM90_TMA_LOAD_MULTICAST.",
        "Preserve ascending-k + first-k ScaleOut::Zero / rest ScaleOut::One in the hand-written load/mma loop (mirror ss_warpspecialized.hpp:480-554). This is the load-bearing determinism contract; NO split-K, NO cross-CTA float reduce, keep single consumer warpgroup per tile (the G==1 path, model_stage_decoder_tc.cuh:88-97). Keep F32BF16BF16_SS (NOT a TF32 atom) so bf16 rounding + fp32 accumulate match the fp64 oracle gate (rel 1e-4).",
        "Map the megakernel's 256-thread (2 warp-group) layout to PipelineTmaAsync Params{role,is_leader,num_consumers}: producer warpgroup issues TMA (elect_one_sync), consumer warpgroup runs cute::gemm. Today the TC megakernel runs wgmma on threads 0..127 with NO asymmetric setmaxnreg (fused_decoder_megakernel.cuh:343-348) — adopting the producer/consumer split (like tile_pipeline.cuh) is the natural CuTe fit but is a launch-layout change that MUST be re-validated against the parity gate.",
        "smem budget: CuTe needs the smem ring (A 64x16 + B Nx16 bf16 per stage x Stages) + pipeline mbarriers. Today DecTcSmem ~17.5KB static under 48KB cap (fused_decoder_megakernel.cuh:355-364,427-429). If the CuTe smem exceeds the static cap, opt into dynamic smem (cudaFuncAttributeMaxDynamicSharedMemorySize) AND re-run the occupancy>=1 hang-freedom guard (fused_decoder_megakernel.cuh:309-321) — 1 CTA/SM must still place or the GridBarrier hangs.",
