      "findings": [
        "No prior agent digests existed in /workspace/cute_plan/ — this is a from-scratch synthesis from an exhaustive read of the live code + CUTLASS v3.6.0 (third_party/cutlass/include/cutlass/version.h: MAJOR=3 MINOR=6 PATCH=0).",
        "Hand-rolled engine to replace: csrc/backends/cuda/sm_90/wgmma.cuh (646 lines, ns sg::sm90::wgs). Key pieces: WgmmaAccum<N> N/2 fp32 regs (wgmma.cuh:314-324); make_desc_A/B_kmajor LBO=MN*16 SBO=128 no-swizzle INTERLEAVE layout idx(mn,k)=(k/8)*(MN*8)+mn*8+(k%8) (wgmma.cuh:255-288, ships kSwizzleNone, 128B-swizzle is a flagged TODO at :156-165); wgmma_issue_n{8..128}<ScaleD,TransA,TransB> per-N inline-asm (:441-561, ships TransA=0/TransB=0); wgmma_frag_decode AUTHORITATIVE thread->(row,col) decode shared by epilogue+gate (:343-364); wgmma_mainloop_kchain ascending-k k=0 overwrite/k>0 accumulate (:617-644 = the determinism contract).",
        "Actual consumer is csrc/fused/sm_90/model_stage_decoder_tc.cuh::tc_gemm_block_unpipelined<N,MaxAtomsM,SrcA,SrcB,Out> (687-1130): token-tiled M=kTileM=128 (kAtomsM=2 stacked m64 atoms), kIL=2 M-atom interleave (726-762), already has cp.async double-buffer + deep ring + a PIPE=2 producer/consumer mbarrier engine selected by SG_TUNED_DEC_FWD_PIPE in {0,1,2} (249-255,860-1062). issue_k ascending-k (750-762). Epilogue uses wgs::wgmma_frag_decode (1097-1101).",
        "dW=dY^T*X uses lambda (transposed-strided) sources -> !kRingAsync -> synchronous scalar gather; the code itself says this 'needs TMA-with-transpose; out of scope' (model_stage_decoder_tc.cuh:782-783). THIS is the single biggest win TMA unlocks.",
        "CUTLASS atoms confirmed available: GMMA SS atoms are spelled cute::SM90::GMMA::MMA_64xNx16_F32BF16BF16_SS (mma_sm90_gmma.hpp:2247-3060; the prompt's SM90_64xNx16_* is the older alias). Swizzle smem layouts GMMA::Layout_K_INTER_Atom<bf16> (no swizzle = the hand layout) and Layout_K_SW128_Atom<bf16> (mma_traits_sm90_gmma.hpp:78-121). SM90_TMA_LOAD::copy = single cp.async.bulk.tensor.2d.shared::cluster.global.mbarrier::complete_tx::bytes (copy_sm90_tma.hpp:95-117,277). Host descriptor via make_tma_copy(SM90_TMA_LOAD{},gtensor,slayout,cta_tiler,Int<1>{}) -> CUtensorMap (copy_traits_sm90_tma.hpp:1268-1302; copy_sm90_desc.hpp:257).",
        "CRITICAL: the TMA PTX is shared::cluster-scoped but works at IMPLICIT cluster-size-1 — NO cluster launch needed. The only requirement is an init'd mbarrier + arrive.expect_tx(tx_bytes), which the project's OWN Mbarrier already issues (warp_specialize.cuh:98-106). So TMA load is device-callable inside the persistent kernel WITHOUT cutlass::PipelineTmaAsync.",
        "Why PipelineTmaAsync canNOT be used verbatim: include/cutlass/pipeline/sm90_pipeline.hpp:271-628 depends on cutlass::arch::ClusterBarrier (274) and cute::cluster_shape()/block_rank_in_cluster/multicast counts (310,342-368,522) — assumes a cluster-launched kernel. The megakernel does plain <<<grid,block>>>, 1 CTA/SM, owns its hand-built GridBarrier. -> reject the collective, adopt the device ATOMS (consistent with wgmma.cuh:16-18 Appendix-B CollectiveMma rejection).",
        "1-CTA/SM hard constraint enforced by launch_fused_decoder_megakernel_tc (fused_decoder_megakernel.cuh:1512): cudaOccupancyMaxActiveBlocksPerMultiprocessor must return >=1 else cudaErrorLaunchOutOfResources (1540-1545). Grid=n_sms (1547), block=SG_TC_MEGA_BLOCK=256 (2 warpgroups). PersistentContext (megakernel_common.cuh:263-276) carries g_next_task/g_arrived/g_generation/n_tasks/n_ctas and is the host->kernel seam for TMA descriptors. GridBarrier sense-reversing, no cooperative launch (147-255).",
        "Gates to preserve (tests/hw/test_decoder_tc.py): _TC_LOSS_REL=1e-4 fp64-oracle loss (:534); grad rel<=2e-2 vs bf16-rounded fp64 oracle (:255,392-459); test_determinism_bitwise A/A/A via torch.equal x3 (:233-245). Plus tests/hw/test_wgmma_substrate.py + csrc/fused/sm_90/decoder_tc_selftest.cu per-orientation micro-gates. Determinism holds BY CONSTRUCTION if: same GMMA atom (CuTe ::fma emits identical wgmma PTX), same ascending-k k=0-overwrite/k>0-accumulate, no-swizzle smem bytes identical, reuse wgs::wgmma_frag_decode -> bit-identical to hand path.",
        "CuTe accumulator (partition_fragment_C) is N/2 fp32 regs/thread — SAME footprint as WgmmaAccum<N> -> no NEW register cost from the MMA swap; the occupancy risk is CuTe Tensor/Layout addressing bloat, mitigated by driving Atom::fma with hand-built make_gmma_desc instead of per-k TiledMMA::partition. Verify with -Xptxas -v before flipping defaults; the >=1-CTA/SM cert is the runtime backstop."
