      ],
      "plan_notes": [
        "Three flags, all default 0 so OFF == byte-identical shipped PTX: SG_TUNED_GEMM_ENGINE (0=hand wgmma, 1=CuTe atoms), SG_TUNED_GEMM_TMA (sub-flag: 0=CuTe MMA + keep cp.async staging to de-risk MMA swap from TMA swap, 1=add SM90_TMA_LOAD), SG_TUNED_GEMM_SWIZZLE (0=Layout_K_INTER no-swizzle byte-identical smem, 1=Layout_K_SW128).",
        "Per-k device sequence (ascending k): (1) if TMA: elect_one_sync leader does Mbarrier::arrive_expect_tx(bytes) then SM90_TMA_LOAD::copy(desc,mbar,0,smem,crd_mn,crd_k=k*16) for A and B, consumers try_wait(parity); else reuse cp_async_cg_16 into the SAME Layout_K_INTER offsets. (2) make_gmma_desc<Major::K> from the smem tensor (replaces make_desc_A/B_kmajor). (3) wgs::wgmma_fence once, then Atom::fma(descA,descB,fragC, k==0?ScaleOut::Zero:ScaleOut::One) per kIL=2 atom into independent fragments sharing one B desc, then wgmma_commit_group + wgmma_wait_group<0>. (4) epilogue reuses wgs::wgmma_frag_decode + out(row,col,v) with if(col<n_real) ragged guard.",
        "Reuse the proven ring: TilePipeline<N,Depth> full/empty Mbarrier ring is single-CTA/cluster-free, composes with TMA directly (producer arrive_expect_tx for TMA bytes instead of cp.async). The PIPE=2 producer/consumer split already exists (model_stage_decoder_tc.cuh:860-987); swap only its cp.async producer body for SM90_TMA_LOAD::copy + arrive_expect_tx, consumer (mbarrier wait + MMA) unchanged. Depth=2 default keeps smem/occupancy at the shipped value.",
        "Determinism preserved by construction: CuTe ::fma emits identical wgmma.mma_async PTX as wgmma_issue_n128 (same hardware reduction); ascending-k k=0 overwrite/k>0 accumulate unchanged; TMA reorders only WHEN a tile lands not the issue order (same invariant the cp.async ring + PIPE=2 engine already keep, :876-886); no-swizzle smem bytes identical; reuse wgs::wgmma_frag_decode (one validated source of truth) -> torch.equal A/A/A and fp64 rel-1e-4 pass. dW split-K stays the deterministic ascending-chunk reduce (:96-101).",
        "Incremental landing, each fully green before next: 4.0 scaffolding OFF (PTX-diff byte-identical); 4.1 ENGINE=1/TMA=0/SWIZZLE=0 route ONLY dectc_gemm_fwd<128> through CuTe MMA atoms + cp.async + reuse frag_decode (gate fwd micro + test_fwd_random/identity + test_determinism_bitwise + full-cell parity); 4.2 flip TMA=1 for fwd (build fwd weight+acts descriptors); 4.3 expand to dX (C1-T transposed cache); 4.4 dW with a transpose-encoding TMA descriptor (removes the scalar gather, the 'out of scope' path 782-783; validate LAST vs test_dw_identity_who_owns_what); 4.5 flip SWIZZLE=1 perf phase (re-run A/A/A at swizzled config); 4.6 generalize to vit/mamba.",
        "Host descriptor creation: make_tma_copy(SM90_TMA_LOAD{}, gtensor=make_tensor(make_gmem_ptr(bf16_base), make_layout(make_shape(rows,K),make_stride(K,1))), slayout=tile_to_shape(Layout_K_INTER_Atom<bf16>{},Shape<TILE_MN,16>{}), cta_tiler, Int<1>{}); extract raw 128B CUtensorMap via tma.get_tma_descriptor(); cudaMemcpy into a device buffer; pass pointer via ctx.g_tma_desc. Descriptors: per-weight-matrix fwd (DecWBf in_w/out_w/ff0_w/ff2_w rows=Nout K=Kin), per-weight dX (transposed *_wT rows=Kin K=Nout), per-acts-region (DecActs X_*/dY_* rows=T K=d/3d/dff) — a few dozen, cached keyed on (base,rows,K) and rebuilt when B/d changes.",
        "Risks: (1) CuTe register bloat — check -Xptxas -v before default flip, drive Atom::fma with hand-built make_gmma_desc not per-k partition, >=1-CTA/SM cert is runtime backstop. (2) CUtensorMap lifetime — cache+rebuild on (base,rows,K) change, assert before launch (stale desc = silent wrong reads). (3) dW transpose-via-TMA is the subtle part (box/stride swap for Major-K core matrices) — validate LAST. (4) swizzle changes smem bytes, re-run A/A/A per-config. (5) needs CUDA>=12 cuTensorMapEncodeTiled (repo targets 12.4, available), guard host builder so non-sm90/old-CUDA still compiles with ENGINE OFF. (6) no cluster but TMA PTX says shared::cluster — valid at implicit cluster-size-1; multicast is explicitly out of scope (1 CTA/SM hard constraint)."
      ],
